  "green-lantern": {
    "pitch": "Green Lantern is a mantle carried by heroes like Hal Jordan and John Stewart. Their rings turn willpower into weapons, shields, and anything else they can imagine in defense of their sector.",
    "overview": [
      "Hal Jordan was a test pilot when a dying alien, Abin Sur, entrusted him with a power ring and responsibility for Earth’s sector. The ring made Hal part of the Green Lantern Corps, an interstellar force whose members use willpower to give their ideas physical form.",
      "John Stewart started as a relief Lantern and grew into a Corps leader. His background as an architect shapes how he builds constructs, which is one of the clearest examples of how the same ring can look and feel different in different hands. The guide separates the people who carry the mantle from alternate realities and transformations."
    ],
    "sources": [
      {
        "label": "DC’s Hal Jordan profile",
        "url": "https://www.dc.com/characters/green-lantern"
      },
      {
        "label": "DC’s John Stewart profile",
        "url": "https://www.dc.com/characters/john-stewart"
      }
    ],
    "reading": {
      "gl-secret-origin": {
        "note": "Start here to see how a test pilot inherits both a ring and a duty from Abin Sur. The collection gives you the basic relationship between Hal, Earth’s sector, and the Corps before the larger crossover stories.",
        "url": "https://www.dc.com/characters/green-lantern"
      },
      "gl-rebirth": {
        "note": "This is the bridge into Geoff Johns’s Green Lantern era. Hal’s return sets up the ongoing 2005 series. Readers who want to understand why his return matters can start with Emerald Twilight and then come back here.",
        "url": "https://www.dc.com/comics/green-lantern-2005/green-lantern-1"
      },
      "sinestro-corps-war": {
        "note": "Sinestro recruits an army that draws its power from fear. The collection crosses between the two Lantern series, making it a good next read once you know the Corps and want to see how its individual members operate in a war.",
        "url": "https://www.dc.com/graphic-novels/green-lantern-2005/green-lantern-the-sinestro-corps-war"
      },
      "blackest-night": {
        "note": "The conflict widens when a new Corps raises dead heroes and villains. This is the central event collection; its companion books follow battles that happen alongside it, so start here before deciding how far into the tie-ins you want to go.",
        "url": "https://www.dc.com/graphic-novels/blackest-night-2009/blackest-night"
      }
    },
